###############################################################################
# Session secrets — never commit these
#
# Two of the extension's own features write secrets to disk, both under these
# default filenames:
#
#   * "Export…"                     -> the 5-byte RC4 key for every session
#   * "Export validation fixtures…" -> the GDay/Mate handshake randoms, which
#                                      are exactly what the keys are derived from
#
# Either file is enough to decrypt the traffic it came from, so they are treated
# the same as any other credential material.
###############################################################################
oracle-forms-keys.json
oracle-forms-fixtures.json
src/test/resources/fixtures/

### Claude Code (machine-local settings) ###
.claude/settings.local.json

### IntelliJ ###
# Ignored wholesale rather than file-by-file: misc.xml pins a specific JDK name
# and language level that will not match another machine, and none of it is
# needed to build (Gradle is the source of truth).
.idea/

